      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Aberration correction made electron microscopy a substantially more powerful instrument for observing matter atom by atom.",
        "attribution": "Rose supplied essential theoretical foundations; Haider and Krivanek delivered distinct, highly influential practical correction systems.",
        "maturity": "Its performance and impact across microscopy, materials science, and nanoscience are long established.",
