      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Titanium-sapphire and practical passive mode locking made robust femtosecond lasers widely available, enabling much of modern ultrafast science.",
        "attribution": "Moulton's laser medium and the passive-mode-locking advances associated with Keller and Sibbett form a coherent instrumental contribution.",
        "maturity": "The experimental platform is exceptionally mature and has enabled generations of measurements.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The broad history of femtosecond-laser development makes a three-person attribution restrictive."
